  "lineage": "Ozan Arif — complete self-described half-hour solo voice and bağlama intermission programmes on Black Sea theatre tours, circa1970–72. First-person interview distinguishes his own programme between the two play acts; actors and later separately described radio artists are outside that bounded solo practice. One human vocal performer and one self-played lute are retained. No archival recording, exact setlist or measured source sound is claimed. Broad balladPoetry scopes the documented lyric-centered solo bard practice. Authored medium mulberry-bowl steel-string bağlama with microtonal frets and ornamented melodic gesture; these construction and articulation choices are a proposed rendition, not measured source equipment. Existing aşık tradition fits the first-person bard practice without transferring Alevi ritual or unrelated named concert performers. All17 human voice controls retained, one accompanied lead with source-unspecified sung/spoken text-setting, physiology and pitch organization. No invented temperament or amplification circuitry. Spacious shoebox-hall listening presentation is editorial, not the historic theatre acoustics.",
